d":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Capture the collapse-engine design decision (core-git fast-import over filter-repo; interleaved ledger reconciliation vs post-pass) in an ADR or design-doc update, not only in regenerated CLI help.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5d","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["T5e","T7"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Step 5 documents only 'regenerate committed CLI help/reference and exit-code documentation artifacts'","Scope makes a load-bearing design choice: 'using core-git git fast-import (NOT third-party git filter-repo ... portability)' and step 3's 'interleaved ... not as a sequential post-pass' rationale","Existing ADR 0106 is cited for horizon/boundary but not for the collapse-engine design itself"],"finding":"The plan introduces a novel below-horizon collapse rewrite engine with a specific design (core-git fast-import over filter-repo; interleaved ledger reconciliation during commit construction rather than a post-pass) but only plans to regenerate CLI help/reference/exit-code artifacts — no ADR or design-doc captures the engine's own architectural decisions.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f13ae5d820ad1f697","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Implementation plan step 5; Scope","norm_id":"n71d06de2ab1ffb08","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future maintainer of S2 (publish/swap) needs to understand why fast-import and interleaved reconciliation were chosen"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a step to record a short ADR (or extend ADR 0106) documenting the fast-import choice and the no-second-rewrite-pass ledger invariant.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State how fast-import failure is detected and surfaced (nonzero exit propagated as an error/exit code) and confirm --apply leaves the branch unadvanced on failure so a re-run is safe.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5d","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Step 6: 'The engine writes only a scratch ref during dry-run and deletes/recreates it each run; --apply advances only the current branch inside that marked clone'","No statement about detecting/surfacing a nonzero git fast-import exit or a partially-written import stream"],"finding":"The engine performs write operations (fast-import object creation, scratch-ref writes, --apply branch advance) but the plan does not state how a fast-import FAILURE mid-run is surfaced or how partial state is left safe/idempotent beyond the disposable-clone blast radius.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fbda24853343f1960","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Implementation plan step 6; step 2","norm_id":"na0338acd73ceb97c","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["git fast-import aborts partway (malformed stream, disk, interrupted) during --apply"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a test case (extend refusal/error-path tests) asserting that a failing fast-import run reports a nonzero exit code and does not advance the branch.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify in step 3 how a ledger position that resolves to the same commit being emitted or to a not-yet-replayed later commit is handled under single-pass interleaving (e.g. such positions fall through to enforce_since grandfathering / content-addressable re-resolution rather than a rewritten SHA), so the 'no second pass' invariant and C5 no-dangling guarantee are both provably satisfied.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7413,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Step 3: 'above-boundary positions map as their commits are replayed' — but a commit's new SHA is only known AFTER fast-import emits it, so the old->new map cannot contain the current or any later commit at the moment its own SNAPSHOT tree is finalized.","A SNAPSHOT ledger entry's position can be introduced by its own carrying commit (a SNAPSHOT event folds events and records positions, potentially including the folding commit's own position); fast-import computes the commit SHA from the tree, creating a chicken-and-egg for self-referential position.commit_sha.","ADR 0106 C4 offers enforce_since grandfathering as the fallback, but step 3 presents interleaving as complete and claims no post-pass is needed, leaving the unresolvable-at-emit-time case unstated."],"finding":"Step 3's single-pass interleaving does not specify how a ledger position resolves when it maps to the SAME commit currently being emitted (self-reference) or to a later not-yet-replayed commit, whose new SHA does not exist at tree-build time.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff6e7697f54196800","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Implementation plan, step 3 ('before emitting each SNAPSHOT-carrying tree, resolve each invariant ledger position ... embed the final position.commit_sha ... No second rewrite pass re-emits a tree after SHAs have been finalized')","norm_id":"n770369dfac7efcfd","priority":0.0587,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A SNAPSHOT whose authorship_ledger position.commit_sha points at the SNAPSHOT's own carrying commit above the boundary.","A retained SNAPSHOT referencing a position first introduced by a topologically-later replayed commit."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add to step 3 that a position whose introducing commit is at-or-above the currently-emitting commit (new SHA not yet finalized) is intentionally left carrying its content-addressable ledger entry and covered by the C4 enforce_since re-anchor, and note that positions only ever resolve backward (to the checkpoint or an already-emitted retained commit) because the reducer replays oldest->newest — confirming no forward SHA is ever required.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2222,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Acknowledge the git-version canonicalization caveat for git fast-import and state why the reduced-form equality check and direct-object-read approach make the rewrite deterministic across supported git versions.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'using core-git git fast-import (NOT third-party git filter-repo ... portability)'","git-filter-repo FAQ (github.com/newren/git-filter-repo/blob/main/Documentation/FAQ.md): 'git fast-export and git fast-import do various canonicalizations of history ... different versions of Git installed can result in differences in filtering.'","Plan mitigates by reading raw objects directly and comparing reduced reducer-state, but the caveat is not stated."],"finding":"The plan chooses git fast-import over git filter-repo but does not acknowledge the documented prior-art caveat that fast-import/fast-export apply git-version-dependent canonicalizations, which bears directly on the 'bit-identical in reduced form' equality AC and on SHA reconstruction determinism.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb2b05f3a45abf8d4","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Implementation plan step 2; Portability section; AC 'Above-horizon history ... bit-identical in reduced form'","norm_id":"n9d5a75e8ee25a1af","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A shadow clone rewritten under a different git version than the eventual S2 apply produces divergent trees/SHAs.","The reducer-state equality fixture passes locally but the rewrite is non-portable across CI git versions."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"50d5261900c7b768","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["8938b51c4209f4f7",6106],"description_boxes":["399141be1d30ac26",0],"file_impact":["b0180cdc08432ccd",9],"ticket_id":["affb514204bf167e",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":711008,"cache